# Build context for the ROOT-context images — frontend/internal and frontend/public.
# (The backend builds from ./backend and has its own backend/.dockerignore.)
#
# Written 2026-08-28. Until then there was no .dockerignore at all, so every root-context build
# uploaded the whole working tree to the daemon: `node_modules`, `.git`, and — the one that
# actually mattered — a 52 MB `frontend/public/.next` from the host. That last one is not merely
# slow: it lands in the image at exactly the path `next build` writes to, and
# `.next/routes-manifest.json` is where the frozen API rewrite lives. A stale host build sitting
# under the real one is the same trap that produced the ECONNREFUSED bug on 2026-08-27.
#
# ⚠️ Deny-list, not an allow-list, and deliberately so: the Dockerfiles COPY specific paths, so
# an over-eager `*` + re-include would fail at build time in a way that is tedious to debug.
# When adding a rule, check it against what those two Dockerfiles actually copy:
#   package.json, package-lock.json, packages/**, frontend/internal/**, frontend/public/**

# --- Dependencies and build output ------------------------------------------
# Host installs are the wrong platform (native binaries built for Windows/macOS) and the
# image reinstalls from the lockfile anyway.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# --- Secrets. Never bake these into an image --------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/appsettings.*.local.json
infra/secrets

# --- The backend. Not copied by either root-context Dockerfile --------------
# It has its own context (./backend); including it here only inflates the upload.
backend

# --- Version control, CI and tooling ----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.impeccable
.agents
.mcp.json
.lsp-mcp.json

# --- Documentation and design sources ---------------------------------------
# `design/` is the source of truth for the UI, but the apps are built from
# `frontend/**` and `packages/**` — the kit itself is never compiled in.
docs
design
marketing
scripts
*.md
LICENSE

# --- Docker's own files ------------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
